1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,460
NVIDIA's price is made six and a half hours a day.

2
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:10,989
On Solana, its token trades all 168 hours of the week…

3
00:00:11,049 --> 00:00:16,314
and 63% of that volume happens while the price isn't

4
00:00:16,374 --> 00:00:17,440
being made.

5
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,817
Those are the hours pools are thinnest.

6
00:00:21,877 --> 00:00:26,632
Over a weekend, prices drift about eight times further

7
00:00:26,692 --> 00:00:31,447
from the stock than on a weekday, and for some names a

8
00:00:31,507 --> 00:00:34,478
round trip costs over one percent.

9
00:00:34,538 --> 00:00:36,440
You pay for the noise.

10
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:42,178
Meet Ade. It's late at night in Lagos, and New York is

11
00:00:42,238 --> 00:00:44,955
shut. She wants $200 of NVIDIA.

12
00:00:45,015 --> 00:00:49,883
SESSION shows both choices: swap now on Jupiter, or buy

13
00:00:49,943 --> 00:00:53,198
at the next open. She picks the bell.

14
00:00:53,258 --> 00:00:57,319
One signature, and her dollars wait in escrow,

15
00:00:57,379 --> 00:01:01,440
cancellable until two minutes before the open.

16
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:07,026
9:30 in New York. The Bell oracle posts NVIDIA's opening

17
00:01:07,086 --> 00:01:11,629
print, and the program verifies its signature on-chain,

18
00:01:11,689 --> 00:01:14,139
with Pyth's own verifier code.

19
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:18,072
Everyone in the cross trades at that one price.

20
00:01:18,132 --> 00:01:22,674
Buyers and sellers net for free, and market makers fill

21
00:01:22,734 --> 00:01:26,440
whatever is left, at a fee the backstop caps.

22
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:32,172
Then, the receipt. The price, and the print behind it,

23
00:01:32,232 --> 00:01:36,645
its signature checked again right in your browser.

24
00:01:36,705 --> 00:01:39,777
What each side put in and got back.

25
00:01:39,837 --> 00:01:44,429
And beside it, what Jupiter would have given at that

26
00:01:44,489 --> 00:01:49,440
moment, because a saving you can't check isn't a saving.

27
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:54,829
Tokenized stocks come with issuer powers, so we drilled

28
00:01:54,889 --> 00:01:59,237
them at a real bell. A pause held the tokens but never

29
00:01:59,297 --> 00:02:03,808
the refunds. A multiplier change cancelled the cross and

30
00:02:03,868 --> 00:02:08,134
refunded everyone, whole. Both escrows ended at zero.

31
00:02:08,194 --> 00:02:12,705
And across 300 random crosses, every balance matched, to

32
00:02:12,765 --> 00:02:13,440
the atom.

33
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:18,581
It belongs on Solana. Signatures verified inside the

34
00:02:18,641 --> 00:02:23,147
same transaction. One instruction clears the whole book,

35
00:02:23,207 --> 00:02:27,714
whatever its size. Token multipliers read on-chain, so a

36
00:02:27,774 --> 00:02:30,895
token's price always matches the share.

37
00:02:30,955 --> 00:02:35,217
And it travels: a Blink on X, or an AI agent with its

38
00:02:35,277 --> 00:02:36,440
limits in code.

39
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:42,187
Today it runs on devnet, at the real New York bells,

40
00:02:42,247 --> 00:02:47,220
with a test signer standing in for Pyth until our Pyth

41
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:51,974
Pro key arrives. Next: an audit, then mainnet, with

42
00:02:52,034 --> 00:02:52,440
caps.

43
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:57,440
SESSION. Trade at the bell.
